#: website/templates/docs.html:34
msgid "How atp2osm works, and how to contribute."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:40
msgid "What is a “brand”?"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:45
#, python-format
msgid "The notion of a <strong>brand</strong> comes straight from <a href=\"%(atp)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">All The Places</a> (ATP). ATP is a collaborative database built around <strong>national and international chains</strong>: retail chains, restaurant networks, banks, pharmacy chains… Every chain is identified there by a unique <a href=\"%(wikidata)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">Wikidata</a> code — for instance <a href=\"%(zara)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link font-mono text-xs\">Q37158</a> for Zara. <strong>Independent shops</strong> (the bakery around the corner, a local restaurant…) are not part of it."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:49
msgid "A few key terms"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:53
msgid "A program dedicated to a single chain, which automatically collects its data from its official website (opening hours, phone, address…)."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:57
msgid "The technique of automatically extracting information from web pages. It is what every ATP spider does to gather the data of a chain."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:63
msgid "atp2osm follows that structure and integrates the data <strong>chain by chain</strong>, faithfully to the ATP spiders. This guarantees that all the data of one chain comes from a single, homogeneous source — which is what makes it possible to judge the quality of a spider by reviewing a random sample of 3 POIs per integrated batch, and to extend that confidence to the whole dataset."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:68
msgid "A chain is missing? Its ATP spider may not exist yet."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:71
msgid "Report it in the missing brands"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:75
msgid "Write a spider on GitHub"
msgstr ""

