#: website/templates/docs.html:114
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:116
#, python-format
msgid "<strong>atp2osm</strong> enriches OpenStreetMap from the <a href=\"%(atp)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">All The Places</a> (ATP) data. ATP automatically collects the information of points of interest (opening hours, phone, website, email) straight from the official websites of the chains."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:119
msgid "The tool compares that data against the existing OSM nodes, finds the missing tags, and lets you review then integrate them into OSM through your own account. <strong>No node is ever created or deleted</strong> — only missing tags are added."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:124
msgid "The process in detail"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:128
msgid "Collecting the ATP data"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:129
msgid "Every week, the latest ATP data is downloaded from alltheplaces.xyz. It holds the POIs with the attributes extracted from the official websites of the chains."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:134
msgid "Refreshing the OSM data"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:135
msgid "In parallel, the OSM data is imported into the local database through osm2pgsql."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:140
msgid "Spatial and attribute matching"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:142
msgid "Every ATP POI is matched against the OSM nodes within <strong>500 m</strong>, checking that at least one attribute is shared among <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">brand:wikidata</span>, <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">brand</span>, <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">name</span>, <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">phone</span>, <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">website</span>, <span class=\"font-mono text-xs\">email</span>. Ambiguous matches — several OSM nodes for one ATP POI — are dropped."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:148
msgid "Computing the missing tags"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:149
msgid "For every match kept, the tool computes which tags exist in ATP but not in OSM. Only the missing ones are offered — <strong>an existing tag is never changed.</strong>"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:154
msgid "Review and integration"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:155
msgid "You check the changes offered for a brand, then you trigger the automatic integration of the whole dataset. The changes are sent to the OSM API through your account, grouped by subdivision."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:162
msgid "How to contribute"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:167
msgid "Sign in with your OSM account"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:168
msgid "Use the sign-in button at the bottom of the menu. Your integrations are recorded under your name in the OSM changeset history."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:174
msgid "Pick a brand"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:175
#, python-format
msgid "The <a href=\"%(link)s\" class=\"link link-primary\">Brands to integrate</a> page lists every chain for which enrichments are available, with the number of nodes concerned."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:181
msgid "Check the matches"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:183
msgid "For every node, check that the ATP ↔ OSM match is right: location, name of the place, tags offered. When in doubt, open the ATP source or the OSM object before accepting."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:191
msgid "If the data looks right, start the integration. The changesets are created automatically on OSM, one per subdivision. The operation cannot be undone: make sure you have checked the data."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:198
msgid "Reviewing a brand"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:200
msgid "Only <strong>3 items at the very least</strong> are reviewed by hand per batch, drawn at random among the places of that batch."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:203
msgid "The review goes <strong>batch by batch</strong>: a brand is cut into batches of whole subdivisions, and before integrating a batch you check a sample drawn at random from it. If that sample is right, the data is considered reliable for every place of the batch."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:206
msgid "The sample holds <strong>at least one example of every tag the batch changes</strong>: if the batch adds, say, <code>phone</code>, <code>website</code>, <code>opening_hours</code> and <code>email</code>, the sample will hold a POI carrying each of them. Every tag is therefore seen at least once before the integration, and the sample is filled at random up to 3 items when it holds fewer. Depending on the tags involved, you may well have <strong>4 POIs to check</strong>, or more."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:209
msgid "Before accepting, make sure the items you checked are representative: try several places in different areas, look at the edge cases (unusual opening hours, badly formatted phone numbers, redirected URLs…). If the slightest doubt remains about the quality of the spider, report an error rather than accept."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:214
msgid "Integration statuses"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:216
#, python-format
msgid "Every integration recorded in the <a href=\"%(link)s\" class=\"link link-primary\">history</a> is given a status reflecting its outcome."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:223
msgid "Integration succeeded"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:225
msgid "Every change has been sent to OpenStreetMap and is now publicly visible."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:236
msgid "Integration partly succeeded"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:239
msgid "Some subdivisions could not be integrated because of an OpenStreetMap API error. The changes that were sent are visible on OSM all the same. The data left out stays available for a later integration."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:250
msgid "Integration cancelled — data reported"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:253
msgid "The integration was stopped after a contributor found errors in the ATP data. Nothing was sent to OpenStreetMap."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:263
msgid "Technical error"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:265
msgid "An error unrelated to what you did stopped the integration. Nothing was sent to OpenStreetMap. You can start the integration again from the page of the brand concerned after 4 weeks. That delay leaves time to fix the errors the datasets may hold."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:274
msgid "Licences"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:279
#, python-format
msgid "The OSM data is published under the <a href=\"%(odbl)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">ODbL 1.0</a> (Open Database License). Every contribution made through this tool falls under the OpenStreetMap <a href=\"%(terms)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">Contributor Terms</a>."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:285
#, python-format
msgid "The ATP data is published under <a href=\"%(cc0)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">CC0 1.0</a> (public domain). It can be used freely, without restriction."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:291
#, python-format
msgid "The source code of this tool is published under the <a href=\"%(gpl)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">GPL-3.0</a> licence. Contributions are welcome on <a href=\"%(github)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">GitHub</a>."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:298
msgid "Exporting the data"
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:303
#, python-format
msgid "The data <strong>produced by atp2osm</strong> can be exported freely, as CSV or JSON, without signing in. It is only the trace of the integrations and the list of the missing brands: the source data stays with the projects that produce it (<a href=\"%(atp)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">All The Places</a> and <a href=\"%(osm)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"link link-primary\">OpenStreetMap</a>)."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:309
msgid "One row per integration: brand, contributor, date, status, number of objects and of tags."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:313
msgid "The detail per changeset: administrative subdivision, number of objects, OSM changeset identifier and status."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:317
msgid "The brands reported as missing from ATP. The ones ATP now knows are left out, unless <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">?show_in_atp=1</code> is passed."
msgstr ""

#: website/templates/docs.html:322
msgid "Replace <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">.csv</code> with <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">.json</code> for the same content as JSON. The <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">history</code> and <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">todo</code> exports take the same filters as their pages (<code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">q</code>, <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">status</code>, <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">user</code>, <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">from</code>, <code class=\"font-mono text-xs\">to</code>) — the “Export” button above each table carries the active filters over anyway."
msgstr ""

